{"id":"refine_20260929114959184","summary":"Saved the validated Continual-ARC rule for task-fb60f9a8 as a global memory.","rationale":"Three demos establish the same pixelwise comparison rule, and the test was solved by comparing corresponding cells rather than marking cells based on the second panel alone.","expectedOutcome":"On future instances of this task, identify the equal-sized panels and separator, compare aligned cells, and produce the panel-sized equality mask; validate that matches are color 3 and nonmatches use the maximum color in the first panel.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_fb60f9a8_pixelwise_panel_equality","title":"Continual-ARC task-fb60f9a8: pixelwise equality between panels","content":"Global, verified Continual-ARC rule for task-fb60f9a8. The input contains two equal-sized panels separated by a full row or column. Remove the separator and compare corresponding cells. Output has the dimensions of either panel: write 3 wherever the two aligned cell values are equal; otherwise write the maximum numeric color present in the first panel (top panel for horizontal layout, left panel for vertical layout). Do not merely mark cells based on their value in the second panel; equality must be pixelwise between both panels. Verified across three demos and a solved test.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The rule is consistent across three demonstrations and correctly predicted the test output after an initial mistaken interpretation.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_fb60f9a8_pixelwise_panel_equality","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-fb60f9a8: pixelwise equality between panels","content":"Global, verified Continual-ARC rule for task-fb60f9a8. The input contains two equal-sized panels separated by a full row or column. Remove the separator and compare corresponding cells. Output has the dimensions of either panel: write 3 wherever the two aligned cell values are equal; otherwise write the maximum numeric color present in the first panel (top panel for horizontal layout, left panel for vertical layout). Do not merely mark cells based on their value in the second panel; equality must be pixelwise between both panels. Verified across three demos and a solved test.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:05.453Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:05.453Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115333668","summary":"Corrected the global task-09778df1 memory to identify target markers by their isolated singleton role rather than assuming they are always color 1.","rationale":"The task was solved after two demos showed target marker colors vary across instances; the exemplar can include background-colored cells, and stamping preserves the source exemplar.","expectedOutcome":"Future solutions should infer the exemplar and target marker color from each grid instead of relying on a fixed marker color; validate by checking the inferred stamp alignment and preserving its source.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_09778df1_stamp_exemplar_at_1_markers","title":"Continual-ARC task-09778df1: copy inferred stamp to isolated singleton markers","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-09778df1: infer the full rectangular stamp/exemplar from the non-marker pattern; its dimensions may vary, and background-valued cells inside its rectangle are part of the stamp. Identify the isolated singleton target markers from the grid rather than assuming a fixed marker color: solved examples used target color 1, while demos used 8 and 5. Copy the stamp centered on each target marker, replacing the marker, and preserve the original exemplar. Verified example: background 8; exemplar at rows 2–4, columns 7–9 was [[8,8,4],[1,4,3],[4,4,4]], centered on 4; copy it to the two isolated 5 markers. A prior failed attempt assumed the wrong marker color and extracted the wrong source patch.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Corrects the earlier over-specific marker-color assumption using a solved instance and two demos.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_09778df1_stamp_exemplar_at_1_markers","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-09778df1: stamp exemplar at 1 markers","content":"Verified on task-09778df1. Infer a small colored exemplar/stamp from the non-marker pattern, then copy it centered on each isolated 1 marker, replacing the marker; preserve the exemplar itself. Demo evidence: seed was a vertical [8,1,1] motif; each 3 target became [8,1,1] vertically, centered on the former 3. For the solved test, the stamp was the 3x3 patch [[4,5,5],[8,5,8],[8,5,0]] (center cell 5), copied center-aligned at every isolated 1; background-valued cells in the stamp are part of the copy. Use task-specific evidence as a strong clue for future fresh inputs under this task id.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:45:55.448425+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:45:55.448441+00:00","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_09778df1_stamp_exemplar_at_1_markers","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-09778df1: copy inferred stamp to isolated singleton markers","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-09778df1: infer the full rectangular stamp/exemplar from the non-marker pattern; its dimensions may vary, and background-valued cells inside its rectangle are part of the stamp. Identify the isolated singleton target markers from the grid rather than assuming a fixed marker color: solved examples used target color 1, while demos used 8 and 5. Copy the stamp centered on each target marker, replacing the marker, and preserve the original exemplar. Verified example: background 8; exemplar at rows 2–4, columns 7–9 was [[8,8,4],[1,4,3],[4,4,4]], centered on 4; copy it to the two isolated 5 markers. A prior failed attempt assumed the wrong marker color and extracted the wrong source patch.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:45:55.448425+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:53:39.239Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115446810","summary":"Saved the verified task-d7ce8437 shape-stamping rule as a global memory.","rationale":"One demonstration establishes the rare-color shape and zero-cell match rule, and the resulting overlay solved the test instance.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, infer the marker shape from its occupied offsets, place it at each in-bounds translation whose shape cells are all zero, and validate that other cells remain unchanged.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_d7ce8437_stamp_rare_shape_on_zeros","title":"Continual-ARC task-d7ce8437: stamp rare-color shape on zeros","content":"Verified Continual-ARC rule for task-d7ce8437: infer the rare marker color's shape from its occupied offsets within its bounding box. At every in-bounds translation where all shape positions are input color 0, overlay the marker color at those positions. Leave all other cells unchanged; overlapping matches form a union. Do not constrain non-marker positions inside the bounding box. Verified against one demo and the correctly solved test.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Preserves a task-specific rule verified by the demonstration and successful test submission.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_d7ce8437_stamp_rare_shape_on_zeros","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-d7ce8437: stamp rare-color shape on zeros","content":"Verified Continual-ARC rule for task-d7ce8437: infer the rare marker color's shape from its occupied offsets within its bounding box. At every in-bounds translation where all shape positions are input color 0, overlay the marker color at those positions. Leave all other cells unchanged; overlapping matches form a union. Do not constrain non-marker positions inside the bounding box. Verified against one demo and the correctly solved test.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:54:51.566Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:54:51.566Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115531508","summary":"Saved the verified task-66cef405 row-end recoloring rule as a global memory.","rationale":"Two demonstrations and a correct test support a task-specific rule: recolor the indicated trailing row-end segment to 1 while preserving the rest of the grid.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, identify the partial stripe or contrasting row-end segment from the examples, recolor only that segment to 1, and leave complete rows and unrelated cells unchanged.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_66cef405_recolor_row_end_segments","title":"Continual-ARC task-66cef405: recolor indicated row-end segments to 1","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-66cef405, based on two demonstrations and a correct test. Identify horizontal rows with the task's partial stripe or contrasting row-end segment; recolor only the indicated trailing segment to 1, preserving the rest of each row and all unrelated cells. The segment may be background-valued cells after a partial stripe (as in the test) or a short contrasting-color tail at the far right (as in a demo). Leave complete rows unchanged. Infer the relevant segment from the row pattern rather than assuming a fixed background color.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Two demonstrations and one correct test"},"reason":"Preserves the verified task-specific transformation while accounting for the different row-end patterns shown in the demonstrations and test.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_66cef405_recolor_row_end_segments","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-66cef405: recolor indicated row-end segments to 1","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-66cef405, based on two demonstrations and a correct test. Identify horizontal rows with the task's partial stripe or contrasting row-end segment; recolor only the indicated trailing segment to 1, preserving the rest of each row and all unrelated cells. The segment may be background-valued cells after a partial stripe (as in the test) or a short contrasting-color tail at the far right (as in a demo). Leave complete rows unchanged. Infer the relevant segment from the row pattern rather than assuming a fixed background color.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Two demonstrations and one correct test"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:55:40.022Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:55:40.022Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115619943","summary":"Updated the existing global task-d7ce8437 memory with a fresh accepted recurrence and clarified placement validation.","rationale":"The conversation records a correct submission on a 25x13 grid and verifies that the inferred 5x4 marker shape was stamped wherever its occupied offsets overlay zero cells, without requiring empty bounding boxes.","expectedOutcome":"On future recurrences, infer the marker shape from the current input, test only its occupied offsets for zero-valued placement cells, preserve unrelated cells and original markers, and validate the resulting grid against the demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_d7ce8437_stamp_rare_shape_on_zeros","title":"Continual-ARC task-d7ce8437: stamp rare-color shape on zeros","content":"Verified Continual-ARC rule for task-d7ce8437, with a fresh accepted recurrence. Infer the rare marker color's shape from its occupied offsets within its bounding box; infer it anew on each instance rather than hard-coding dimensions or offsets. At every in-bounds translation where all occupied shape positions overlay input color 0, stamp the marker color at those positions. Only occupied shape positions need to be zero; the whole bounding box need not be zero. Preserve all unrelated cells and original markers. In the accepted 25x13 recurrence, background was 9, marker color was 5, and the inferred 5x4 shape offsets were {(0,2),(1,1),(2,1),(2,2),(3,0),(3,1),(4,2),(4,3)}.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Accepted test recurrence"},"reason":"Record the successful recurrence and explicitly distinguish occupied-cell placement checks from requiring an entirely zero bounding box.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_d7ce8437_stamp_rare_shape_on_zeros","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-d7ce8437: stamp rare-color shape on zeros","content":"Verified Continual-ARC rule for task-d7ce8437: infer the rare marker color's shape from its occupied offsets within its bounding box. At every in-bounds translation where all shape positions are input color 0, overlay the marker color at those positions. Leave all other cells unchanged; overlapping matches form a union. Do not constrain non-marker positions inside the bounding box. Verified against one demo and the correctly solved test.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:54:51.566Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:54:51.566Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_d7ce8437_stamp_rare_shape_on_zeros","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-d7ce8437: stamp rare-color shape on zeros","content":"Verified Continual-ARC rule for task-d7ce8437, with a fresh accepted recurrence. Infer the rare marker color's shape from its occupied offsets within its bounding box; infer it anew on each instance rather than hard-coding dimensions or offsets. At every in-bounds translation where all occupied shape positions overlay input color 0, stamp the marker color at those positions. Only occupied shape positions need to be zero; the whole bounding box need not be zero. Preserve all unrelated cells and original markers. In the accepted 25x13 recurrence, background was 9, marker color was 5, and the inferred 5x4 shape offsets were {(0,2),(1,1),(2,1),(2,2),(3,0),(3,1),(4,2),(4,3)}.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Accepted test recurrence"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:54:51.566Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:56:25.045Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115705648","summary":"Create a global memory for the verified Continual-ARC task-bbe28dbc transformation.","rationale":"Two demonstrations and a correctly solved test support moving the separate object adjacent to a full straight rail, clearing its source, and adding one parallel line of 8 immediately beyond the moved object.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, identify the background, rail, and object; preserve the object's shape and alignment while moving it adjacent to the rail, and add only the single parallel line of 8 on its far side. Validate that the source is cleared and other cells remain unchanged.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_bbe28dbc_move_object_to_rail_and_add_line","title":"Continual-ARC task-bbe28dbc: move object adjacent to rail and add a parallel line","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-bbe28dbc. Identify the uniform background, a full straight line of another color (the rail, horizontal or vertical), and a separate contiguous non-background object. Move the whole object, preserving its shape and colors, to the nearest placement adjacent to the rail on the side toward which it can move, preserving its position along the rail. Clear the object's original cells to background. On the moved object's side away from the rail, paint exactly one complete line of color 8 parallel to the rail, one cell beyond the object's far edge. Do not fill the intervening gap. Keep the rail and all other cells unchanged. Verified with a horizontal rail and two-cell object, a vertical rail and 3x9 object, and a solved test with a horizontal rail and two-cell object.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Two demonstrations and a correctly solved test"},"reason":"The transformation recurred in both horizontal and vertical orientations and was validated on the test.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_bbe28dbc_move_object_to_rail_and_add_line","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-bbe28dbc: move object adjacent to rail and add a parallel line","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-bbe28dbc. Identify the uniform background, a full straight line of another color (the rail, horizontal or vertical), and a separate contiguous non-background object. Move the whole object, preserving its shape and colors, to the nearest placement adjacent to the rail on the side toward which it can move, preserving its position along the rail. Clear the object's original cells to background. On the moved object's side away from the rail, paint exactly one complete line of color 8 parallel to the rail, one cell beyond the object's far edge. Do not fill the intervening gap. Keep the rail and all other cells unchanged. Verified with a horizontal rail and two-cell object, a vertical rail and 3x9 object, and a solved test with a horizontal rail and two-cell object.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Two demonstrations and a correctly solved test"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:57:11.691Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:57:11.691Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115914968","summary":"Saved the verified task-43293a65 periodic-pattern completion rule as a global memory.","rationale":"Four demonstrations and the correctly solved test support completing a periodic motif in the orientation indicated by the seed; the failed symmetry-based guess also shows that reflection should not be assumed.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, identify the seed motif and its orientation, phase-align periodic continuation, and preserve known cells; validate that the completed pattern matches the seed.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_43293a65_periodic_pattern_completion","title":"Continual-ARC task-43293a65: complete periodic patterns in the indicated orientation","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-43293a65, based on four demonstrations and a correctly solved test. Infer the seed pattern's orientation and periodic motif from the nonzero cells, then complete the grid by periodic continuation with the correct phase; preserve known cells. In horizontal-stripe cases, read the seeded rows as a vertical sequence and repeat it cyclically in both directions: [3,9,9,0] completes to [3,9,9,3]; the seed rows [1,9,6] align to the repeating sequence [6,1,9,...]; and the test sequence [0,9,4,0,0] completes to [4,9,4,9,4]. Other examples encode cyclic sequences on diagonal directions, including NW-SE and NE-SW; infer the orientation from the seed and continue periodically along it. Do not assume mirror symmetry: this is periodic completion, not reflection.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Four demonstrations; solved test after an incorrect symmetry-based attempt."},"reason":"Persist a verified, reusable rule for this recurring task, including orientation inference and the caution against the demonstrated symmetry error.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_43293a65_periodic_pattern_completion","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-43293a65: complete periodic patterns in the indicated orientation","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-43293a65, based on four demonstrations and a correctly solved test. Infer the seed pattern's orientation and periodic motif from the nonzero cells, then complete the grid by periodic continuation with the correct phase; preserve known cells. In horizontal-stripe cases, read the seeded rows as a vertical sequence and repeat it cyclically in both directions: [3,9,9,0] completes to [3,9,9,3]; the seed rows [1,9,6] align to the repeating sequence [6,1,9,...]; and the test sequence [0,9,4,0,0] completes to [4,9,4,9,4]. Other examples encode cyclic sequences on diagonal directions, including NW-SE and NE-SW; infer the orientation from the seed and continue periodically along it. Do not assume mirror symmetry: this is periodic completion, not reflection.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Four demonstrations; solved test after an incorrect symmetry-based attempt."},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:59:21.423Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:59:21.423Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115944141","summary":"Saved the verified task-3e640848 transformation as a global memory.","rationale":"The demonstration and correctly accepted test both show the complete foreground pattern shifting down exactly one row while retaining its cell values and leaving the background unchanged.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, identify the background and foreground cells, shift every foreground cell down one row, discard cells that move beyond the grid, and validate the result against the demonstrated translation.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_3e640848_shift_pattern_down_one_row","title":"Continual-ARC task-3e640848: shift the foreground pattern down one row","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-3e640848, supported by one demonstration and a correctly accepted test. Preserve the grid dimensions and background. Translate every foreground cell down exactly one row, preserving its color; cells that move beyond the bottom edge are dropped, and vacated cells are background. The demo used color 1 on background 6; the test used color 0 on background 7. Infer foreground/background from each input rather than assuming fixed colors, and validate by checking the one-row translation of all foreground cell locations.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Persist the verified transformation for future instances of this recurring task.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_3e640848_shift_pattern_down_one_row","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-3e640848: shift the foreground pattern down one row","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-3e640848, supported by one demonstration and a correctly accepted test. Preserve the grid dimensions and background. Translate every foreground cell down exactly one row, preserving its color; cells that move beyond the bottom edge are dropped, and vacated cells are background. The demo used color 1 on background 6; the test used color 0 on background 7. Infer foreground/background from each input rather than assuming fixed colors, and validate by checking the one-row translation of all foreground cell locations.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:59:48.264Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:59:48.264Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120144691","summary":"Saved the verified task-53587865 compartment-pattern replication rule as a global memory.","rationale":"The demonstration shows a pattern copied between two compartments separated by a full-width line, and the correct test submission replicates the populated compartment pattern across a 3×3 arrangement while preserving divider lines.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, identify the equal-sized compartments and their separators, infer the exact pattern from the populated compartment, and replicate it in the others without altering separators or background-valued holes.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_53587865_replicate_pattern_across_compartments","title":"Continual-ARC task-53587865: replicate a pattern across compartments","content":"Verified Continual-ARC rule for task-53587865. Full straight separator lines divide the grid into equal-sized compartments. Infer the exact multicolor pattern in the populated compartment, including relative positions and background-valued holes, and copy it into every other compartment. Preserve the grid dimensions and leave separator lines unchanged. The rule was demonstrated with a 5×8 compartment pattern copied below a full-width divider, and verified on a correct test with a 5×9 pattern replicated across a 3×3 partition formed by two full-width and two full-height separators.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The transformation was verified on a demonstration pair and a correctly accepted test submission.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_53587865_replicate_pattern_across_compartments","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-53587865: replicate a pattern across compartments","content":"Verified Continual-ARC rule for task-53587865. Full straight separator lines divide the grid into equal-sized compartments. Infer the exact multicolor pattern in the populated compartment, including relative positions and background-valued holes, and copy it into every other compartment. Preserve the grid dimensions and leave separator lines unchanged. The rule was demonstrated with a 5×8 compartment pattern copied below a full-width divider, and verified on a correct test with a 5×9 pattern replicated across a 3×3 partition formed by two full-width and two full-height separators.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:49.410Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:49.410Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120925311","summary":"Saved the verified task-1c0718b6 line-completion rule and its key failure-avoidance guidance as a global memory.","rationale":"The accepted test and four demonstrations support completing selected coherent marker tracks, while multiple incorrect submissions show that filling every aligned gap or recursively closing the resulting grid overfills it.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, infer which tracks are selected from the current input, complete vertical tracks before horizontal ones, and avoid unsupported recursive propagation; validate against the demonstrations and preserve unselected gaps.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_1c0718b6_complete_selected_marker_tracks","title":"Continual-ARC task-1c0718b6: complete selected marker tracks","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-1c0718b6, supported by four demonstrations and an accepted test. The grid has a uniform background and sparse markers of another color; add color 2 in gaps along selected coherent horizontal and vertical marker tracks. Infer the selected tracks from each input rather than using a fixed threshold or connecting every pair of collinear markers. Complete vertical tracks first, then horizontal tracks using the vertically added cells; do not recursively propagate horizontal fills back into more columns. The demonstrations show that some lines with only two widely separated markers remain incomplete. In the accepted 19x9 test (background 4, markers 3), add color 2 at row 2 columns 2–3, row 3 column 5, row 4 columns 0–1, row 5 column 0, and row 8 columns 1–2 and 4 (zero-based indexing); leave rows 6–7 between columns 0 and 5 unchanged. Indiscriminate collinear gap-filling and recursive closure that fills a rectangle were both rejected.","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","evidence":"four demonstrations and accepted test"},"reason":"Preserves the verified transformation and guards against the overfilling strategies that produced incorrect submissions.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_1c0718b6_complete_selected_marker_tracks","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-1c0718b6: complete selected marker tracks","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-1c0718b6, supported by four demonstrations and an accepted test. The grid has a uniform background and sparse markers of another color; add color 2 in gaps along selected coherent horizontal and vertical marker tracks. Infer the selected tracks from each input rather than using a fixed threshold or connecting every pair of collinear markers. Complete vertical tracks first, then horizontal tracks using the vertically added cells; do not recursively propagate horizontal fills back into more columns. The demonstrations show that some lines with only two widely separated markers remain incomplete. In the accepted 19x9 test (background 4, markers 3), add color 2 at row 2 columns 2–3, row 3 column 5, row 4 columns 0–1, row 5 column 0, and row 8 columns 1–2 and 4 (zero-based indexing); leave rows 6–7 between columns 0 and 5 unchanged. Indiscriminate collinear gap-filling and recursive closure that fills a rectangle were both rejected.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","evidence":"four demonstrations and accepted test"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:09:33.953Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:09:33.953Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929121113475","summary":"Saved the verified task-10672b2b horizontal-gap-filling rule as a global memory.","rationale":"The demonstration and accepted test both show one-cell gaps between horizontally aligned marker cells being filled with color 2 while all other cells remain unchanged.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, identify same-row marker cells separated by a one-cell gap, fill only those gaps with 2, and preserve the markers and unrelated cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_10672b2b_fill_horizontal_marker_gaps","title":"Continual-ARC task-10672b2b: fill one-cell horizontal marker gaps","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-10672b2b. In a grid with a uniform background and repeated same-row marker cells separated by one cell, fill each intermediate gap cell with color 2. Preserve all marker cells, the background, and unrelated cells. The demonstration used background 8 and markers 4, including a pair and longer horizontal runs; the accepted test used background 9 and markers 3 in several rows. Infer the background and marker colors from each input; fill only the one-cell gaps between horizontally aligned marker cells.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The transformation was confirmed by a demonstration and a correctly accepted test.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_10672b2b_fill_horizontal_marker_gaps","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-10672b2b: fill one-cell horizontal marker gaps","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-10672b2b. In a grid with a uniform background and repeated same-row marker cells separated by one cell, fill each intermediate gap cell with color 2. Preserve all marker cells, the background, and unrelated cells. The demonstration used background 8 and markers 4, including a pair and longer horizontal runs; the accepted test used background 9 and markers 3 in several rows. Infer the background and marker colors from each input; fill only the one-cell gaps between horizontally aligned marker cells.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:11:17.369Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:11:17.369Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929121931200","summary":"Created a global memory for the verified Continual-ARC task-e7a2d445 rule and its key failure-avoidance guidance.","rationale":"The accepted test confirms that a duplicated shape is selected using the large L-shaped marker and recolored to the marker's color; earlier attempts that chose a nearby small L or unrelated component were incorrect.","expectedOutcome":"On future recurrences, identify the large L-shaped marker, compare repeated shapes, and use the marker's indicated region to select the matching copy rather than choosing by proximity alone; validate that only the selected copy changes.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_e7a2d445_select_duplicate_by_L_marker","title":"Continual-ARC task-e7a2d445: use the L marker to select a duplicate shape","content":"Global Continual-ARC memory for task-e7a2d445. Across the demonstrations and accepted test, grids contain a mostly uniform background, a large L-shaped marker, and scattered objects that may include matching or duplicated shapes. Recolor the selected matching object to the large marker's color, using the marker's orientation/position to identify the indicated copy; do not choose merely by proximity. The accepted test directly verifies this selection: the large color-7 L marker indicates one of two identical five-cell color-3 shapes. Recolor only the copy at rows 12–13, columns 11–13 (1-based); leave the copy at rows 27–28, columns 14–16 unchanged. Avoid mistaking a nearby small L-shaped object or an unrelated component for the target: those choices were incorrect in earlier attempts. Treat the duplicated-shape selection as directly validated, and do not infer a more specific general selection formula than the examples support.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Preserves the accepted task rule and the demonstrated caution against proximity-based target selection.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_e7a2d445_select_duplicate_by_L_marker","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-e7a2d445: use the L marker to select a duplicate shape","content":"Global Continual-ARC memory for task-e7a2d445. Across the demonstrations and accepted test, grids contain a mostly uniform background, a large L-shaped marker, and scattered objects that may include matching or duplicated shapes. Recolor the selected matching object to the large marker's color, using the marker's orientation/position to identify the indicated copy; do not choose merely by proximity. The accepted test directly verifies this selection: the large color-7 L marker indicates one of two identical five-cell color-3 shapes. Recolor only the copy at rows 12–13, columns 11–13 (1-based); leave the copy at rows 27–28, columns 14–16 unchanged. Avoid mistaking a nearby small L-shaped object or an unrelated component for the target: those choices were incorrect in earlier attempts. Treat the duplicated-shape selection as directly validated, and do not infer a more specific general selection formula than the examples support.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:19:36.721Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:19:36.721Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929122126721","summary":"Updated the global memory for Continual-ARC task-d7ce8437 with the verified fixed-orientation shape-matching rule.","rationale":"The demo and correctly accepted test confirm that the current marker shape defines an occupied-cell mask within its bounding box; matching translations require zeros only at occupied offsets, while blank mask positions are don't-care.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, infer the marker mask and color from the input, scan same-orientation translations, recolor the occupied cells of every zero-matching placement, and preserve all other cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_d7ce8437_stamp_rare_shape_on_zeros","title":"Continual-ARC task-d7ce8437: match and stamp the marker mask on zeros","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-d7ce8437, confirmed by a demonstration and an accepted test. Infer the non-background marker color and the marker's full bounding-box binary mask from the current input; do not hard-code its dimensions or offsets. Scan all in-bounds translations in the same orientation (do not rotate or reflect). A placement matches when every cell at an occupied mask offset is zero; cells at blank mask offsets are don't-care and may contain any value. Recolor the occupied cells of every matching placement to the marker color. Union the recolored cells when matches overlap, and preserve all other cells, including the source marker and nonzero cells at don't-care offsets.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The accepted test and demo establish the precise matching semantics, including fixed orientation and don't-care bounding-box cells, improving recurrence handling beyond a vague instruction to stamp the shape.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_d7ce8437_stamp_rare_shape_on_zeros","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-d7ce8437: stamp rare-color shape on zeros","content":"Verified Continual-ARC rule for task-d7ce8437, with a fresh accepted recurrence. Infer the rare marker color's shape from its occupied offsets within its bounding box; infer it anew on each instance rather than hard-coding dimensions or offsets. At every in-bounds translation where all occupied shape positions overlay input color 0, stamp the marker color at those positions. Only occupied shape positions need to be zero; the whole bounding box need not be zero. Preserve all unrelated cells and original markers. In the accepted 25x13 recurrence, background was 9, marker color was 5, and the inferred 5x4 shape offsets were {(0,2),(1,1),(2,1),(2,2),(3,0),(3,1),(4,2),(4,3)}.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Accepted test recurrence"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:54:51.566Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:56:25.045Z","version":2},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_d7ce8437_stamp_rare_shape_on_zeros","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-d7ce8437: match and stamp the marker mask on zeros","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-d7ce8437, confirmed by a demonstration and an accepted test. Infer the non-background marker color and the marker's full bounding-box binary mask from the current input; do not hard-code its dimensions or offsets. Scan all in-bounds translations in the same orientation (do not rotate or reflect). A placement matches when every cell at an occupied mask offset is zero; cells at blank mask offsets are don't-care and may contain any value. Recolor the occupied cells of every matching placement to the marker color. Union the recolored cells when matches overlap, and preserve all other cells, including the source marker and nonzero cells at don't-care offsets.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:54:51.566Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:21:33.942Z","version":3},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"