{"id":"refine_20260929122325872","summary":"Updated the global task-fa97545b memory with the verified panel-intersection rule and the failure-avoidance lesson.","rationale":"The accepted test and demonstration confirm that aligned nonzero cells in the two panels produce 2, while every other output cell is 0; earlier incorrect submissions came from treating the more frequent panel color as background.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, identify the equal-sized panels and divider, compare aligned cells for nonzero occupancy, and output 2 only at overlaps; validate the output dimensions against one panel.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_fa97545b_intersect_aligned_non_background_cells_across_divide","title":"Continual-ARC task-fa97545b: intersect aligned non-background cells across divider","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-fa97545b. The input has two equal-sized panels separated by a single uniform divider column; panel dimensions can vary. Compare aligned cells, treating 0 as empty in both panels regardless of which color is most frequent. Output has the dimensions of either panel: write 2 where both aligned input cells are nonzero, and 0 otherwise. Preserve no other input values in the output. Verified by a 6x25 demonstration (left occupied color 6, right occupied color 3) and an accepted 16x27 test (left occupied color 3, right occupied color 9). Failure avoidance: do not infer empty/background cells by panel color frequency; the right panel may be mostly 3 or 9, but its zero cells are still empty. The output width is the panel width, excluding the divider.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Capture the accepted rule and correct the specific background-by-frequency assumption that caused two incorrect submissions.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_fa97545b_intersect_aligned_non_background_cells_across_divide","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-fa97545b: intersect aligned non-background cells across divider","content":"Verified on Continual-ARC task-fa97545b with one demonstration and an accepted test. The input has two equal-width panels aligned row-by-row, separated by a uniform divider column. In the demonstration, the left panel has background 0 and marked cells 3; the right panel has background 0 and marked cells 8 (divider color 6). The output is one panel of the same height and panel width: put color 2 where the corresponding cell in BOTH panels is non-background, and put 0 everywhere else. Equivalently, compute the cellwise intersection of the two non-background masks; do not preserve marker colors. The accepted test used left background 0/marks 5, right background 6/holes 0, and divider 8. Thus non-background means 5 on the left and 6 on the right; output 2 at their aligned intersection and 0 elsewhere. Ignore the divider and remove both panels from the output. Panel width is determined from the two sides of the divider and can vary (demo width 14, test width 5).","path":"continual_arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"task_id":"task-fa97545b","verified":"accepted test after one demo"},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:22:03.137008+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:22:03.137027+00:00","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_fa97545b_intersect_aligned_non_background_cells_across_divide","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-fa97545b: intersect aligned non-background cells across divider","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-fa97545b. The input has two equal-sized panels separated by a single uniform divider column; panel dimensions can vary. Compare aligned cells, treating 0 as empty in both panels regardless of which color is most frequent. Output has the dimensions of either panel: write 2 where both aligned input cells are nonzero, and 0 otherwise. Preserve no other input values in the output. Verified by a 6x25 demonstration (left occupied color 6, right occupied color 3) and an accepted 16x27 test (left occupied color 3, right occupied color 9). Failure avoidance: do not infer empty/background cells by panel color frequency; the right panel may be mostly 3 or 9, but its zero cells are still empty. The output width is the panel width, excluding the divider.","path":"continual_arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:22:03.137008+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:23:32.320Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929122434050","summary":"Updated the global task-53587865 memory with the latest verified panel-replication evidence.","rationale":"The existing memory covers this task, and the two demonstrations plus correct test confirm that a populated compartment’s full pattern is copied into every equal-sized compartment, including background-valued cells.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, identify the full separator lines and equal-sized panels, infer the populated panel, and replicate it exactly while preserving separators; validate panel alignment and dimensions.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_53587865_replicate_pattern_across_compartments","title":"Continual-ARC task-53587865: replicate a pattern across compartments","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-53587865, confirmed by two demonstrations and a correct test. Full uniform straight separator lines divide the grid into equal-sized rectangular compartments. Infer the exact contents of the populated compartment and copy them identically into every other compartment, preserving relative positions, colors, and background-valued cells or holes. Preserve the separator lines and grid dimensions. The source compartment may vary; in the observed examples it was the lower-right panel or the lower panel. Before copying, verify that compartments have matching dimensions and alignment.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Incorporates the latest verified recurrence while clarifying source-panel variability and preservation of background-valued cells.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_53587865_replicate_pattern_across_compartments","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-53587865: replicate a pattern across compartments","content":"Verified Continual-ARC rule for task-53587865. Full straight separator lines divide the grid into equal-sized compartments. Infer the exact multicolor pattern in the populated compartment, including relative positions and background-valued holes, and copy it into every other compartment. Preserve the grid dimensions and leave separator lines unchanged. The rule was demonstrated with a 5×8 compartment pattern copied below a full-width divider, and verified on a correct test with a 5×9 pattern replicated across a 3×3 partition formed by two full-width and two full-height separators.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:49.410Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:49.410Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_53587865_replicate_pattern_across_compartments","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-53587865: replicate a pattern across compartments","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-53587865, confirmed by two demonstrations and a correct test. Full uniform straight separator lines divide the grid into equal-sized rectangular compartments. Infer the exact contents of the populated compartment and copy them identically into every other compartment, preserving relative positions, colors, and background-valued cells or holes. Preserve the separator lines and grid dimensions. The source compartment may vary; in the observed examples it was the lower-right panel or the lower panel. Before copying, verify that compartments have matching dimensions and alignment.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:49.410Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:24:39.618Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929122920763","summary":"Saved the verified task-105dda7b rectangle-restoration rule as a global memory.","rationale":"The task was solved correctly after six demonstrations, and the final attempt fixed an earlier error by extending the lower-left rectangle through its full edge at row 20.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, infer the full extents of the solid colored rectangles, restore corrupted interior cells, and replace stray outside pixels with the uniform background; validate each rectangle's complete boundaries before submitting.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_105dda7b_restore_noisy_rectangles","title":"Continual-ARC task-105dda7b: restore noisy solid rectangles","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-105dda7b, confirmed across six demonstrations and a correctly solved test. The grid has a uniform background and several solid, axis-aligned colored rectangles overlaid with scattered single-cell corruptions/noise. Infer each rectangle's full extent from consistent rows and columns, restore its interior cells to the rectangle's color, and replace stray outside pixels with the background while preserving other clean cells. Carefully trace every rectangle to its complete edge: in the solved test, the lower-left 9 rectangle continued through row 20, one row farther than initially guessed. The bottom 5 patch was a 2x4 rectangle.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Six demonstrations; final test accepted."},"reason":"Preserves the verified transformation and the specific boundary-checking lesson that corrected an earlier wrong submission.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_105dda7b_restore_noisy_rectangles","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-105dda7b: restore noisy solid rectangles","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-105dda7b, confirmed across six demonstrations and a correctly solved test. The grid has a uniform background and several solid, axis-aligned colored rectangles overlaid with scattered single-cell corruptions/noise. Infer each rectangle's full extent from consistent rows and columns, restore its interior cells to the rectangle's color, and replace stray outside pixels with the background while preserving other clean cells. Carefully trace every rectangle to its complete edge: in the solved test, the lower-left 9 rectangle continued through row 20, one row farther than initially guessed. The bottom 5 patch was a 2x4 rectangle.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Six demonstrations; final test accepted."},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:29:27.473Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:29:27.473Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929122949990","summary":"Create a global memory for the verified Continual-ARC task-2a787dfa compartment-counting rule.","rationale":"The rule is supported by a demonstration and a correctly accepted test with different grid layouts and colors.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, detect the compartment separators, count marker cells per compartment, and return the compact compartment grid with 1 only where the count is exactly two.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_2a787dfa_mark_compartments_with_exactly_two_markers","title":"Continual-ARC task-2a787dfa: mark compartments containing exactly two markers","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-2a787dfa. The input grid is partitioned by full-width and/or full-height uniform separator lines into an R-by-C array of equal rectangular compartments. Infer the background and sparse marker colors from the compartments, identify separator rows and columns, and count marker cells within each compartment, excluding separators. Output an R-by-C grid: use color 1 for compartments containing exactly two marker cells, and the background color for all other compartments. Do not return the original-sized grid. Verified demo: a 19x11 grid split by separator rows 4, 9, 14 and columns 2, 5, 8 into sixteen 4x2 compartments; only compartment (row 1, column 3) had exactly two markers, and the 4x4 output marked it with 1. Verified test: a 19x5 grid split into four row bands and two columns; the exactly-two-marker compartments produced [[7,7],[7,1],[7,1],[7,7]], accepted as correct. Count carefully and derive compartment dimensions from the separators rather than assuming a fixed layout.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Captures a reusable transformation confirmed on a demonstration and accepted test with distinct layouts and colors.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_2a787dfa_mark_compartments_with_exactly_two_markers","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-2a787dfa: mark compartments containing exactly two markers","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-2a787dfa. The input grid is partitioned by full-width and/or full-height uniform separator lines into an R-by-C array of equal rectangular compartments. Infer the background and sparse marker colors from the compartments, identify separator rows and columns, and count marker cells within each compartment, excluding separators. Output an R-by-C grid: use color 1 for compartments containing exactly two marker cells, and the background color for all other compartments. Do not return the original-sized grid. Verified demo: a 19x11 grid split by separator rows 4, 9, 14 and columns 2, 5, 8 into sixteen 4x2 compartments; only compartment (row 1, column 3) had exactly two markers, and the 4x4 output marked it with 1. Verified test: a 19x5 grid split into four row bands and two columns; the exactly-two-marker compartments produced [[7,7],[7,1],[7,1],[7,7]], accepted as correct. Count carefully and derive compartment dimensions from the separators rather than assuming a fixed layout.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:29:56.051Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:29:56.051Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929125818730","summary":"Saved the verified Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e transformation as a global memory.","rationale":"Five demonstrations and the accepted test support a rule based on parallel boundary segments, coordinate offsets, recolored markers, and perpendicular rays; the solved test also exposed two useful failure-avoidance details.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, infer the segment orientation, offset, and colors from the input; draw both source-side rays and offset-mapped lines while preserving the boundary segments, then validate against the demonstrated geometry.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_cf412e0e_offset_mapped_perpendicular_rays","title":"Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e: draw offset-mapped perpendicular rays","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e, supported by five demonstrations and an accepted test. Find the two equal-length, parallel colored boundary segments on opposite sides of the grid. Their relative positions define an offset mapping between coordinates along the segments. Recolor each sparse marker to 4. For a marker aligned with one boundary segment, draw the marker's original color along the perpendicular ray toward that same-side boundary, stopping before the marker and preserving the boundary. Map the marker's along-segment coordinate by the offset to the opposite side and draw a full perpendicular line in the marker's original color across the intervening region; fill the inactive-side boundary-edge cell if it is not part of a boundary, but preserve any active boundary segment. The geometry works for horizontal or vertical segments and is independent of background and marker colors. In the accepted test, vertical boundaries were at column 0, rows 1–8, and column 19, rows 9–16: markers in rows 1–8 became 4, drew color 5 leftward to column 1, and produced a full color-5 row across columns 0–18 at row + 8; the active boundary cell at column 19 remained 2. Avoid omitting the source-side ray or leaving the inactive boundary-edge cell unfilled.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Five demonstrations and accepted test"},"reason":"Preserves a verified reusable task rule and the specific mistakes that led to incorrect submissions.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_cf412e0e_offset_mapped_perpendicular_rays","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e: draw offset-mapped perpendicular rays","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e, supported by five demonstrations and an accepted test. Find the two equal-length, parallel colored boundary segments on opposite sides of the grid. Their relative positions define an offset mapping between coordinates along the segments. Recolor each sparse marker to 4. For a marker aligned with one boundary segment, draw the marker's original color along the perpendicular ray toward that same-side boundary, stopping before the marker and preserving the boundary. Map the marker's along-segment coordinate by the offset to the opposite side and draw a full perpendicular line in the marker's original color across the intervening region; fill the inactive-side boundary-edge cell if it is not part of a boundary, but preserve any active boundary segment. The geometry works for horizontal or vertical segments and is independent of background and marker colors. In the accepted test, vertical boundaries were at column 0, rows 1–8, and column 19, rows 9–16: markers in rows 1–8 became 4, drew color 5 leftward to column 1, and produced a full color-5 row across columns 0–18 at row + 8; the active boundary cell at column 19 remained 2. Avoid omitting the source-side ray or leaving the inactive boundary-edge cell unfilled.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Five demonstrations and accepted test"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:29.146Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:29.146Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
