{"id":"refine_20260929130800901","summary":"Create a global memory for the verified Continual-ARC task-201bcb5a transformation.","rationale":"The demo and accepted test show the same rule across different background and marker colors: fill only single-cell horizontal gaps between same-row markers with color 2.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, fill each one-cell horizontal gap between marker cells with 2, preserve all markers and unrelated cells, and avoid filling vertical gaps.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_201bcb5a_fill_single_cell_horizontal_gaps","title":"Continual-ARC task-201bcb5a: fill single-cell horizontal marker gaps","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-201bcb5a. In each row, whenever two marker cells of the same color have exactly one cell between them, replace that intervening background cell with color 2. Preserve all marker cells and all other cells; do not fill vertical gaps or cells not bracketed by such a horizontal marker pair. The marker and background colors may vary: the demo used background 0 and markers 7, while the accepted test used background 3 and markers 8.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The rule was demonstrated with one color pair and confirmed by a correct test using different colors, establishing a reusable task-specific transformation.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_201bcb5a_fill_single_cell_horizontal_gaps","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-201bcb5a: fill single-cell horizontal marker gaps","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-201bcb5a. In each row, whenever two marker cells of the same color have exactly one cell between them, replace that intervening background cell with color 2. Preserve all marker cells and all other cells; do not fill vertical gaps or cells not bracketed by such a horizontal marker pair. The marker and background colors may vary: the demo used background 0 and markers 7, while the accepted test used background 3 and markers 8.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:08:06.657Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:08:06.657Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929131610231","summary":"Saved the verified task-f03c73de shape-matching rule as a global memory.","rationale":"Six demonstrations and the accepted test confirm that the connected marker shape is used in its original orientation to locate exact placements over zero-valued cells; the union of those matches is recolored to the marker color.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, infer the marker mask and color from the input, scan all valid translations without rotating or reflecting it, recolor only exact all-zero matches, and preserve all other cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_f03c73de_stamp_shape_on_zero_matches","title":"Continual-ARC task-f03c73de: recolor exact zero-matches of the marker shape","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-f03c73de, confirmed by six demonstrations and an accepted test. A grid has a two-color background and a connected marker-color shape. Infer the marker color and its exact binary mask from the current input. Scan translations of that mask in its original orientation only; do not rotate or reflect it. A placement matches only when every mask cell overlays a 0. Recolor the mask cells of every exact match to the marker color, taking the union of matches when placements overlap. Preserve the original marker and every other cell. In the accepted test, five exact placements were found.","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","verification":"six demonstrations and accepted test"},"reason":"Persist the repeatedly demonstrated transformation and orientation constraint for future recurrences of this task.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_f03c73de_stamp_shape_on_zero_matches","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-f03c73de: recolor exact zero-matches of the marker shape","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-f03c73de, confirmed by six demonstrations and an accepted test. A grid has a two-color background and a connected marke