{"id":"refine_20260929131747104","summary":"Updated the global memory for Continual-ARC task-8a9e8801 with confirmation from a second correctly solved test.","rationale":"The task rule is already stored globally, and this trajectory reconfirmed it with a 26×29 test using background 9 and marker 5, solved correctly without wrong attempts.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, preserve grid dimensions and cell positions while replacing background cells with 0 and marker cells with the original background color.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_8a9e8801_map_background_to_zero_and_markers_to_background","title":"Continual-ARC task-8a9e8801: map background to zero and markers to background","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-8a9e8801, reconfirmed by a second correctly solved test. For a grid with a uniform background color and sparse pixels of one distinct marker color, output the same dimensions and preserve every cell's position. Replace every background cell with 0 and every marker cell with the original background color. The latest test used background 9 and marker 5 and was solved with no wrong attempts. Do not move, add, or remove pixels; this is a cellwise color mapping.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Record the additional successful test evidence and emphasize the position-preserving color mapping.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_8a9e8801_map_background_to_zero_and_markers_to_background","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-8a9e8801: map background to zero and markers to background","content":"Verified Continual-ARC task-8a9e8801 using its demonstration and solved test. The input is a grid with a uniform background color and sparse pixels of one other color. Output preserves dimensions and positions, changes every background cell to 0, and changes every non-background marker cell to the original background color. In the demo, background 2 became 0 and marker 5 became 2; in the solve