-diagonal r+c=5, color 2 on r+c=22, and color 4 at r+c=27. The smallest consistent rectangular tile was 3×3; the completed pattern followed (r+c) mod 3 = 0 → 4, 1 → 2, 2 → 1. Validate the candidate tile against every known nonzero cell before filling the grid.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:07:23.189Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:20:05.534Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929132244385","summary":"Updated the global task-cf412e0e memory with the verified row-offset stencil rule and its key failure-avoidance guidance.","rationale":"The existing memory covers offset-mapped perpendicular rays, and this instance adds four demonstrations, a correct test, and a failed overgeneralization that painted entire boundary runs. Updating the existing task memory avoids a duplicate and records that only marker-selected row offsets are active.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, project the marker-row stencil onto the relevant boundary runs, paint inward only on active rows, and preserve inactive rows and unrelated cells; validate against the demonstrated hit-marker recoloring to 4.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_cf412e0e_offset_mapped_perpendicular_rays","title":"Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e: project marker-row stencil from boundary runs","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e, supported by four demonstrations and a correctly solved test. In a uniform-background grid, identify contiguous boundary-color runs along one or more vertical edges and sparse marker pixels of a distinct paint color. Use marker rows as an active row-offset stencil relative to the associated boundary run, projecting those offsets to other relevant edge runs. On active rows, extend the paint color horizontally inward from the boundary run through background cells; when a ray hits a marker, recolor that hit marker to 4. Preserve the boundary run and all unrelated cells. Crucial failure avoidance: do not paint every row of a boundary run; paint only rows selected by the marker-derived stencil. In the solved test, boundary-color 1 runs were at right rows 5–10 and left rows 16–21, and the paint-color 8 marker at (5,2) selected offset 0. Only rows 5 and 16 were active: row 5 painted columns 3–4 with 8 and changed the marker at (5,2) to 4; row 16 painted columns 1–5 with 8; other rows remained unchanged. Demonstrations used different backgrounds, boundary colors, and paint colors (including 5, 7, and 2); hit markers became 4.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Four demonstrations and one accepted test; one incorrect submission painted inactive rows."},"reason":"Refine the existing task memory with the verified row-stencil interpretation and guard against the observed overpainting failure.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_cf412e0e_offset_mapped_perpendicular_rays","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e: draw offset-mapped perpendicular rays","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e, supported by five demonstrations and an accepted test. Find the two equal-length, parallel colored boundary segments on opposite sides of the grid. Their relative positions define an offset mapping between coordinates along the segments. Recolor each sparse marker to 4. For a marker aligned with one boundary segment, draw the marker's original color along the perpendicular ray toward that same-side boundary, stopping before the marker and preserving the boundary. Map the marker's along-segment coordinate by the offset to the opposite side and draw a full perpendicular line in the marker's original color across the intervening region; fill the inactive-side boundary-edge cell if it is not part of a boundary, but preserve any active boundary segment. The geometry works for horizontal or vertical segments and is independent of background and marker colors. In the accepted test, vertical boundaries were at column 0, rows 1–8, and column 19, rows 9–16: markers in rows 1–8 became 4, drew color 5 leftward to column 1, and produced a full color-5 row across columns 0–18 at row + 8; the active boundary cell at column 19 remained 2. Avoid omitting the source-side ray or leaving the inactive boundary-edge cell unfilled.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Five demonstrations and accepted test"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:29.146Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:29.146Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_cf412e0e_offset_mapped_perpendicular_rays","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e: project marker-row stencil from boundary runs","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e, supported by four demonstrations and a correctly solved test. In a uniform-background grid, identify contiguous boundary-color runs along one or more vertical edges and sparse marker pixels of a distinct paint color. Use marker rows as an active row-offset stencil relative to the associated boundary run, projecting those offsets to other relevant edge runs. On active rows, extend the paint color horizontally inward from the boundary run through background cells; when a ray hits a marker, recolor that hit marker to 4. Preserve the boundary run and all unrelated cells. Crucial failure avoidance: do not paint every row of a boundary run; paint only rows selected by the marker-derived stencil. In the solved test, boundary-color 1 runs were at right rows 5–10 and left rows 16–21, and the paint-color 8 marker at (5,2) selected offset 0. Only rows 5 and 16 were active: row 5 painted columns 3–4 with 8 and changed the marker at (5,2) to 4; row 16 painted columns 1–5 with 8; other rows remained unchanged. Demonstrations used different backgrounds, boundary colors, and paint colors (including 5, 7, and 2); hit markers became 4.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Four demonstrations and one accepted test; one incorrect submission painted inactive rows."},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:29.146Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:22:52.779Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/a