{"id":"refine_20260929132345881","summary":"Saved the verified task-406e04ad rectangular-perimeter rule as a global memory.","rationale":"Two demonstrations and the correctly solved test support the same transformation: use the bounding box of the non-background marker cells and color its perimeter with 2, preserving existing markers and all cells outside the perimeter.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, identify the marker color and its bounding box, recolor only background cells on the bounding-box perimeter to 2, and preserve all other cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_406e04ad_draw_marker_bounding_box_perimeter","title":"Continual-ARC task-406e04ad: draw the marker bounding-box perimeter","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-406e04ad, supported by two demonstrations and a correctly solved test. In a grid with a uniform background and sparse pixels of one distinct marker color, find the minimum bounding rectangle containing all marker pixels. On the rectangle's perimeter, change background cells to color 2 and preserve any marker pixels already there. Leave all cells off the perimeter unchanged. The background and marker colors vary across examples; the added perimeter color remains 2. Do not fill the rectangle's interior.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"This concise, recurrence-specific rule is verified by both demonstrations and the accepted test.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_406e04ad_draw_marker_bounding_box_perimeter","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-406e04ad: draw the marker bounding-box perimeter","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-406e04ad, supported by two demonstrations and a correctly solved test. In a grid with a uniform background and sparse pixels of one distinct marker color, find the minimum bounding rectangle containing all marker pixels. On the rectangle's perimeter, change background cells to color 2 and preserve any marker pixels already there. Leave all cells off the perimeter unchanged. The background and marker colors vary across examples; the added perimeter color remains 2. Do not fill the rectangle's interior.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:23:53.036Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:23:53.036Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929133415702","summary":"Updated the global task-6244d383 memory to replace blanket row-suffix filling with selective completion based on corresponding repeated rows.","rationale":"The prior rule caused three incorrect submissions. The accepted solution and demos 4–8 show that only selected missing trailing cells are filled, according to foreground in corresponding pattern rows; internal gaps and unrelated rows must be preserved.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, compare corresponding rows in repeated horizontal pattern groups and fill only qualifying trailing background cells with 1. Validate that internal gaps, existing foreground, and unrelated rows remain unchanged.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_6244d383_fill_right_of_rowwise_last_foreground","title":"Continual-ARC task-6244d383: selectively complete missing trailing cells in corresponding pattern rows","content":"Global verified guidance for Continual-ARC task-6244d383, replacing the incorrect blanket row-suffix rule. In repeated horizontal pattern groups, identify corresponding reference and shortened rows, then fill with 1 only those missing trailing-background cells in one row where the corresponding reference row has foreground. Preserve existing foreground, internal gaps, leading cells, and rows outside the matching pattern. Do not fill every cell east of each row's rightmost foreground, and do not paint internal background gaps after the first foreground. Demos 4–8 confirm suffix-only completion of repeated patterns; the copy to complete can be earlier or later, so compare counterparts rather than assuming a top/bottom direction. In the accepted test, changes were limited to the bottom pattern: row 22, columns 19–24 (1-based), and row 23, columns 19, 21, and 23. Row 23 columns 18, 20, 22, and 24 remained unchanged because the corresponding reference row had background there. The task-specific method for identifying corresponding rows or repeated pattern groups may require inference; retain that uncertainty.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Accepted test and demos 4–8; previous blanket rule caused three incorrect submissions."},"reason":"Replace a disproven global rule with the selective counterpart-based behavior supported by the accepted solution and demonstrations.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_6244d383_fill_right_of_rowwise_last_foreground","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-6244d383: fill each row east of its rightmost non-background cell with 1","content":"Verified on task-6244d383 with two demonstrations and a correctly solved test. Let the uniform background be the most common color. For each row independently, find the rightmost cell that is not background; replace every background cell to its right through the grid's right edge with color 1. Preserve all cells at or left of that rightmost non-background cell, and leave fully background rows or rows whose rightmost non-background cell is already at the right edge unchanged. Demo 1 (background 6, marker/object 8): rows 7-9 had rightmost 8 at column 15 and the sole following cell (column 16) became 1; rows 18-20 already reached the edge and did not change. Demo 2 (background 2, foreground 7): partial horizontal bars on rows 6 and 10 were extended to the right edge in color 1; full-width bars stayed unchanged. Test (background 3, color 4): row 6 had 4 in columns 0-13, so columns 14-24 became 1; full-width row 13 stayed unchanged. The rule applies row-wise even when the foreground pattern is not a simple contiguous stripe.","path":"continual_arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"task_id":"task-6244d383","version":1,"verified_demos":2,"verified_test":1},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:24:40.890214+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:24:40.890243+00:00","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_6244d383_fill_right_of_rowwise_last_foreground","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-6244d383: selectively complete missing trailing cells in corresponding pattern rows","content":"Global verified guidance for Continual-ARC task-6244d383, replacing the incorrect blanket row-suffix rule. In repeated horizontal pattern groups, identify corresponding reference and shortened rows, then fill with 1 only those missing trailing-background cells in one row where the corresponding reference row has foreground. Preserve existing foreground, internal gaps, leading cells, and rows outside the matching pattern. Do not fill every cell east of each row's rightmost foreground, and do not paint internal background gaps after the first foreground. Demos 4–8 confirm suffix-only completion of repeated patterns; the copy to complete can be earlier or later, so compare counterparts rather than assuming a top/bottom direction. In the accepted test, changes were limited to the bottom pattern: row 22, columns 19–24 (1-based), and row 23, columns 19, 21, and 23. Row 23 columns 18, 20, 22, and 24 remained unchanged because the corresponding reference row had background there. The task-specific method for identifying corresponding rows or repeated pattern groups may require inference; retain that uncertainty.","path":"continual_arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Accepted test and demos 4–8; previous blanket rule caused three incorrect submissions."},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:24:40.890214+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:34:24.084Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929133618862","summary":"Create a global memory for the verified Continual-ARC task-4d6ec835 shape-matching recolor rule.","rationale":"The test submission was accepted, and three demonstrations consistently show a designated object recolored to the key color associated with an exact matching component shape while unrelated objects remain unchanged.","expectedOutcome":"On future recurrences, compare component shapes, infer the replacement color from the matching reference, and recolor only the designated target; validate that unrelated cells are preserved.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_4d6ec835_recolor_designated_shape_match","title":"Continual-ARC task-4d6ec835: recolor the designated exact shape match","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-4d6ec835. The grid contains colored components, including a structured reference/key pattern and a designated target component whose shape matches another component. Recolor only the designated target to the key color indicated by the matching reference; preserve all other cells and components. Compare component shapes exactly, including holes and cell arrangement, rather than matching by bounding-box size alone. Evidence: in the solved 18×18 test, the color-9 component at rows 6–7, columns 3–7 has shape [##### / #.###], matching the color-4 component at rows 0–1, columns 0–4; the target color-9 component is recolored to 7 and the submission was correct. Demonstrations show analogous mappings: a designated 9 shape [## / ###] becomes 0; a 7 shape [## / #.] becomes 6, matching a color-2 shape; and a designated 7 shape [#### / ##.# / #### / ####] becomes 5, matching a color-9 shape. Do not blanket-recolor all objects of a color or select an incidental shape match without using the structured pattern to identify the intended target and replacement color.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"three demonstrations and one accepted test"},"reason":"T