{"id":"refine_20260929133806997","summary":"Create a global memory recording the verified rectangle-restoration rule for Continual-ARC task-27794c88.","rationale":"Two demonstrations and a correctly solved test support restoring multiple solid monochrome rectangles of different colors, while removing sparse noise and preserving the uniform background.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, identify each rectangle's color and full bounds, restore corrupted cells within it, and reset isolated noise outside rectangles to the background; validate against the observed rectangle extents.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_27794c88_restore_multiple_noisy_rectangles","title":"Continual-ARC task-27794c88: restore multiple noisy solid rectangles","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-27794c88, supported by two demonstrations and a correctly solved test. The grid has a uniform background and multiple solid, axis-aligned monochrome rectangles, potentially in different colors, with sparse arbitrary-color corruption both inside and outside the rectangles. Infer each rectangle's exact bounding box and fill every cell within it with that rectangle's color. Set cells outside the rectangles, including isolated noise marks, to the uniform background. Do not assume there is only one target color: the demonstrations preserve rectangles of colors 6, 4, and 2 on backgrounds 1 or 5; the solved test preserves rectangles of colors 8 and 1 on background 0. Infer extents from coherent repeated rows and columns, and preserve all distinct rectangles.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Two demonstrations and accepted test"},"reason":"This is a stable, task-specific transformation rule verified across demonstrations and a correct test.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_27794c88_restore_multiple_noisy_rectangles","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-27794c88: restore multiple noisy solid rectangles","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-27794c88, supported by two demonstrations and a correctly solved test. The grid has a uniform background and multiple solid, axis-aligned monochrome rectangles, potentially in different colors, with sparse arbitrary-color corruption both inside and outside the rectangles. Infer each rectangle's exact bounding box and fill every cell within it with that rectangle's color. Set cells outside the rectangles, including isolated noise marks, to the uniform background. Do not assume there is only one target color: the demonstrations preserve rectangles of colors 6, 4, and 2 on backgrounds 1 or 5; the solved test preserves rectangles of colors 8 and 1 on background 0. Infer extents from coherent repeated rows and columns, and preserve all distinct rectangles.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Two demonstrations and accepted test"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:38:13.130Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:38:13.130Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929134011879","summary":"Created a global memory for the verified task-dc4ef19a enclosed-cavity fill rule.","rationale":"One demonstration and a correctly solved test show that background cells inside closed orthogonal outlines are recolored, while outlines and unrelated background remain unchanged.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, identify genuinely enclosed cavities and recolor their interiors to 4; validate that open shapes and exterior background are preserved.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_dc4ef19a_fill_enclosed_outline_cavities","title":"Continual-ARC task-dc4ef19a: fill enclosed outline cavities","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-dc4ef19a, supported by one demonstration and a correctly solved test. In a grid with a background and orthogonal outlines made of a line color, recolor every background cell strictly inside any completely enclosed outline cavity to color 4. Preserve the outline and all other cells. Check that each candidate cavity is actually closed; do not fill open shapes or unrelated background. The demo's enclosed one-cell-wide vertical cavity and both enclosed cavities in the test were filled.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"one demonstration and one correctly solved test"},"reason":"Preserves a verified task-specific transformation and its key boundary condition for future task recurrence.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_dc4ef19a_fill_enclosed_outline_cavities","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-dc4ef19a: fill enclosed outline cavities","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-dc4ef19a, supported by one demonstration and a correctly solved test. In a grid with a background and orthogonal outlines made of a line color, recolor every background cell strictly inside any completely enclosed outline cavity to color 4. Preserve the outline and all other cells. Check that each candidate cavity is actually closed; do not fill ope