ss two demonstrations and two correctly solved tests. The grid has a uniform background and a complete straight divider of color 2. Find the colored object/segment immediately on one side of the divider. Add a full-length stripe of color 8 one cell beyond the object's bounding extent, on the side away from the divider, parallel to the divider; preserve all original cells and dimensions. In demo 1, the vertical divider was at column 5 and a color-1 segment occupied column 4, so output added color 8 in column 3 for every row. In demo 2, the horizontal divider was at row 20 and the color-7 shape reached row 19, so output added row 13 (one beyond its topmost extent) entirely in color 8. Solved test 1: vertical divider at column 1, color-7 shape spanning columns 2–3 adjacent to its right, so add a full-height color-8 stripe at column 4. Solved test 2: in a 25×27 grid (zero-based indices), the full-height color-2 divider was at column 26 and the color-5 object touched it from the left, spanning columns 23–25; add a full-height color-8 stripe at column 22, one cell beyond the object's bounding box away from the divider. Do not overwrite object or divider cells.","path":"continual_arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","task_id":"task-42a857dc","version":2,"verified":"two demonstrations and two correctly solved tests"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:57:58.191164+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:03:02.888Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929140549405","summary":"Updated the global task-cf412e0e memory with the verified ray rule and the failed-attempt lesson.","rationale":"Four demonstrations and an accepted test establish perpendicular rays from border stripes, with active positions determined by the target pixels’ exact projected coordinates; the first test attempt failed by using a contiguous range instead.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, preserve stripe cells, project the exact active offsets, recolor ray cells appropriately, stop at target pixels while changing them to 4, and validate orientation and untouched cells against the input.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_cf412e0e_offset_mapped_perpendicular_rays","title":"Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e: project marker-row stencil from boundary runs","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e, supported by four demonstrations and a correctly solved test. In a uniform-background grid, identify distinctive stripe runs along one or more borders and sparse target-color pixels. Cast rays perpendicular inward from the stripes at the active offsets indicated by the target pixels' positions projected onto the stripe axis; use the exact occupied offset set, not the first N positions. Recolor traversed background cells to the target color. If a ray reaches a target pixel, change that pixel to 4 and stop that ray there. Preserve stripe cells, unaligned target pixels, and all other cells. Stripes can be horizontal or vertical, and may occur on opposite borders. Validate the ray orientation, projected offset set, stopping/recoloring behavior, and unchanged cells. A failed test attempt used a contiguous range of offsets; the accepted solution used the exact set, including its gap.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Preserves the demonstrated general rule and a directly observed failure-avoidance lesson for future recurrences.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_cf412e0e_offset_mapped_perpendicular_rays","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e: project marker-row stencil from boundary runs","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e, supported by four demonstrations and a correctly solved test. In a uniform-background grid, identify contiguous boundary-color runs along one or more vertical edges and sparse marker pixels of a distinct paint color. Use marker rows as an active row-offset stencil relative to the associated boundary run, projecting those offsets to other relevant edge runs. On active rows, extend the paint color horizontally inward from the boundary run through background cells; when a ray hits a marker, recolor that hit marker to 4. Preserve the boundary run and all unrelated cells. Crucial failure avoidance: do not paint every row of a boundary run; paint only rows selected by the marker-derived stencil. In the solved test, boundary-color 1 runs were at right rows 5–10 and left rows 16–21, and the paint-color 8 marker at (5,2) selected offset 0. Only rows 5 and 16 were active: row 5 painted columns 3–4 with 8 and changed the marker at (5,2) to 4; row 16 painted columns 1–5 with 8; other rows remained unchanged. Demonstrations used different backgrounds, boundary colors, and paint colors (including 5, 7, and 2); hit markers became 4.\n\nAdditional verified recurrence: on a 21×27 grid with background 8, color-9 edge runs were left rows 4–11 and right rows 13–20. Color-3 markers on rows 4, 6, 7, 9, 10, 11 selected offsets 0, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7 within the left run. Each active left-edge ray painted rightward through background up to its marker; the hit marker became 4. The same offsets mapped to the right run activated rows 13, 15, 16, 18, 19, 20, which were painted leftward across the remaining row cells. The task was solved correctly on the first submission. This confirms that the stencil can contain several nonconsecutive offsets, and each active ray proceeds toward the opposite edge unless stopped by a marker.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Four demonstrations and one accepted test; one incorrect submission painted inactive rows."},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:29.146Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:39:41.166021+00:00","version":3},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_cf412e0e_offset_mapped_perpendicular_rays","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e: project marker-row stencil from boundary runs","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-cf412e0e, supported by four demonstrations and a correctly solved test. In a uniform-background grid, identify distinctive stripe runs along one or more borders and sparse target-color pixels. Cast rays perpendicular inward from the stripes at the active offsets indicated by the target pixels' positions projected onto the stripe axis; use the exact occupied offset set, not the first N positions. Recolor traversed background cells to the target color. If a ray reaches a target pixel, change that pixel to 4 and stop that ray there. Preserve stripe cells, unaligned target pixels, and all other cells. Stripes can be horizontal or vertical, and may occur on opposite borders. Validate the ray orientation, projected offset set, stopping/recoloring behavior, and unchanged cells. A failed test attempt used a contiguous range of offsets; the accepted solution used the exact set, including its gap.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:29.146Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:05:58.609Z","version":4},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929140649475","summary":"Updated the global memory for Continual-ARC task-a2bb13dc with the verified reflected expansion rule.","rationale":"The trajectory includes two demonstrations and a correctly solved test, establishing the output dimensions and both reflection directions.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, produce a 3H×2W grid by emitting source rows in reverse, forward, then reverse order, and mirror each row before appending the original; validate dimensions and row order.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_a2bb13dc_reflected_tiling","title":"Continual-ARC task-a2bb13dc: expand by reflected tiling (general, verified)","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-a2bb13dc, confirmed by two demonstrations and a correctly solved test. For an H×W input A, produce a 3H×2W output. Emit input rows in this order: reversed row order (bottom to top), original row order (top to bottom), then reversed row order again. For each emitted row, concatenate its horizontal reversal followed by the original row. Thus the output consists of three vertical bands with row-order pattern reversed/forward/reversed; each band uses a left-to-right mirrored copy followed by the original. Preserve cell colors exactly. Validate output dimensions (3H rows, 2W columns), the row-band order, and each mirrored-plus-original row.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Replaces the earlier provisional description with the precise transformation confirmed by two demonstrations and the accepted test.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_a2bb13dc_reflected_tiling","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-a2bb13dc: expand by reflected tiling (general, v2)","content":"Global task-specific memory for Continual-ARC task-a2bb13dc. The demonstrated 8×6 input expands to a 24×12 output (3H×2W) using the previously recorded reflected-copy arrangement. Preserve that arrangement as provisional: its precise orientation is supported by only one nonuniform demonstration. An additional accepted test used the uniform 2×1 input [[2],[2]] and produced a 6×2 output filled with 2s. This confirms the 3H×2W dimensions but cannot distinguish or provide evidence for any tile orientations. Do not treat the uniform test as orientation evidence.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:00:43.541Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:05:44.515Z","version":2},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_a2bb13dc_reflected_tiling","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-a2bb13dc: expand by reflected tiling (general, verified)","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-a2bb13dc, confirmed by two demonstrations and a correctly solved test. For an H×W input A, produce a 3H×2W output. Emit input rows in this order: reversed row order (bottom to top), original row order (top to bottom), then reversed row order again. For each emitted row, concatenate its horizontal reversal followed by the original row. Thus the output consists of three vertical bands with row-order pattern reversed/forward/reversed; each band uses a left-to-right mirrored copy followed by the original. Preserve cell colors exactly. Validate output dimensions (3H rows, 2W columns), the row-band order, and each mirrored-plus-original row.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:00:43.541Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:06:55.808Z","version":3},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929141759245","summary":"Create a global memory for the verified Continual-ARC task-adc3b04d rule and its input-validation lesson.","rationale":"Eight demo pairs with horizontal and vertical dividers and a correctly solved test establish the panel-comparison rule; a failed attempt also showed that an omitted input value can shift comparisons and create false matches.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, identify the divider and compare aligned panel cells without transforming them, using the shared palette color for unequal pairs and 3 for equal pairs; validate row widths and panel alignment before submitting.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_adc3b04d_compare_panels_equal_cells","title":"Continual-ARC task-adc3b04d: mark equal aligned panel cells","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-adc3b04d, supported by eight demo pairs with horizontal and vertical dividers and a correctly solved test. Find the full single-color divider separating two equal-sized panels, remove it, and compare corresponding cells directly, without rotation or reflection. Write 3 where the aligned values are exactly equal; otherwise write the sole color shared by the two panels' palettes. Preserve the panel dimensions. Validation lesson: check every input row has its stated width and confirm the divider index and panel slices before comparing; a transcription omission can shift a panel and create false equality marks.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Persist the verified task rule and the concrete transcription failure lesson to improve future recurrences.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_adc3b04d_compare_panels_equal_cells","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-adc3b04d: mark equal aligned panel cells","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-adc3b04d, supported by eight demo pairs with horizontal and vertical dividers and a correctly solved test. Find the full single-color divider separating two equal-sized panels, remove it, and compare corresponding cells directly, without rotation or reflection. Write 3 where the aligned values are exactly equal; otherwise write the sole color shared by the two panels' palettes. Preserve the panel dimensions. Validation lesson: check every input row has its stated width and confirm the divider index and panel slices before comparing; a transcription omission can shift a panel and create false equality marks.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:18:05.143Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:18:05.143Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929142147619","summary":"Updated the existing global memory for Continual-ARC task-406e04ad with confirmation and the additional horizontal-row completion rule.","rationale":"Four demonstrations and a correctly solved test confirm that the rule completes the foreground bounding-box perimeter in color 2 while preserving foreground pixels. The solved test and demo 4 also show completion of a horizontal row containing a multi-pixel internal run; demo 2 confirms an already complete outline can remain unchanged.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, complete the marker bounding-box perimeter and the indicated horizontal row, preserving original markers and grid dimensions; validate the bounds and each changed cell.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_406e04ad_draw_marker_bounding_box_perimeter","title":"Continual-ARC task-406e04ad: complete marker bounding-box perimeter and indicated row","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-406e04ad, confirmed by four demonstrations and a correctly solved test. In a uniform-background grid with sparse pixels of one foreground color, find their bounding box and complete its rectangular perimeter by changing background cells on the perimeter to color 2; preserve all original foreground pixels and all cells outside the operation. Also complete the indicated horizontal row spanning the bounding-box width when it contains a multi-pixel internal foreground run, filling only gaps with 2. In the solved test the bounds were rows 2–16 and columns 5–26, and row 13 was completed across that width. Demo 4 showed the analogous completion of row 9. Demo 2 had an already complete rectangular outline and was unchanged. Validate dimensions, bounding-box limits, and preservation of original foreground cells.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds recurrence evidence and a verified row-completion detail to the existing task-specific memory.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_406e04ad_draw_marker_bounding_box_perimeter","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-406e04ad: draw the marker bounding-box perimeter","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-406e04ad, supported by two demonstrations and a correctly solved test. In a grid with a uniform background and sparse pixels of one distinct marker color, find the minimum bounding rectangle containing all marker pixels. On the rectangle's perimeter, change background cells to color 2 and preserve any marker pixels already there. Leave all cells off the perimeter unchanged. The background and marker colors vary across examples; the added perimeter color remains 2. Do not fill the rectangle's interior.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:23:53.036Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:23:53.036Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_406e04ad_draw_marker_bounding_box_perimeter","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-406e04ad: complete marker bounding-box perimeter and indicated row","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-406e04ad, confirmed by four demonstrations and a correctly solved test. In a uniform-background grid with sparse pixels of one foreground color, find their bounding box and complete its rectangular perimeter by changing background cells on the perimeter to color 2; preserve all original foreground pixels and all cells outside the operation. Also complete the indicated horizontal row spanning the bounding-box width when it contains a multi-pixel internal foreground run, filling only gaps with 2. In the solved test the bounds were rows 2–16 and columns 5–26, and row 13 was completed across that width. Demo 4 showed the analogous completion of row 9. Demo 2 had an already complete rectangular outline and was unchanged. Validate dimensions, bounding-box limits, and preservation of original foreground cells.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:23:53.036Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:21:56.234Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929142324063","summary":"Saved the verified task-5d71124a motif-stamping rule as a global memory.","rationale":"One demonstration and a correctly solved test support identifying a compact motif and stamping its non-background cells around each marker, while leaving motif-background cells untouched.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, infer the motif and marker from the input, align the motif’s bounding-box center with each marker, preserve background-valued motif positions and the original motif, and keep grid dimensions unchanged.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_5d71124a_stamp_motif_at_markers","title":"Continual-ARC task-5d71124a: stamp motif centered on markers","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-5d71124a, confirmed by one demonstration and a correctly solved test. In a uniform-background grid, identify the compact colored motif and its bounding box, including background-colored cells within that box, plus the scattered marker pixels. Stamp the motif centered on each marker by aligning the motif bounding-box center cell with the marker. Write only motif cells whose color differs from the background; background-valued positions in the motif are transparent and must not overwrite the grid. Preserve the original motif and all unrelated cells; keep the grid dimensions unchanged. In the demonstration, a three-cell vertical motif with colors [7,5,5] on background 9 was centered on each marker of color 6. In the test, the motif was [[3,6,1],[9,3,7],[6,5,5]] on background 5, centered on each 0 marker. Do not assume fixed motif dimensions or colors.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"This task-specific transformation was demonstrated and the inferred rule produced an accepted test output.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_5d71124a_stamp_motif_at_markers","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-5d71124a: stamp motif centered on markers","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-5d71124a, confirmed by one demonstration and a correctly solved test. In a uniform-background grid, identify the compact colored motif and its bounding box, including background-colored cells within that box, plus the scattered marker pixels. Stamp the motif centered on each marker by aligning the motif bounding-box center cell with the marker. Write only motif cells whose color differs from the background; background-valued positions in the motif are transparent and must not overwrite the grid. Preserve the original motif and all unrelated cells; keep the grid dimensions unchanged. In the demonstration, a three-cell vertical motif with colors [7,5,5] on background 9 was centered on each marker of color 6. In the test, the motif was [[3,6,1],[9,3,7],[6,5,5]] on background 5, centered on each 0 marker. Do not assume fixed motif dimensions or colors.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:23:32.659Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:23:32.659Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929143048246","summary":"Replace the overconfident task-4d6ec835 memory with an explicitly unresolved account of the demonstrations and failed test hypotheses.","rationale":"The existing global memory asserts a solved L-key shape-matching rule, but this trajectory provides eight demonstrations with varied recolorings and eight incorrect test guesses, so that rule is not established.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, treat the selection rule as unresolved, use fresh demonstrations to infer it, and avoid repeating the known failed transformations; validate any candidate against every demo before applying it.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_4d6ec835_recolor_designated_shape_match","title":"Continual-ARC task-4d6ec835: unresolved component recoloring associated with an L-shaped key","content":"Global task memory; rule unresolved. Across eight demonstrations, exactly one non-background connected component is recolored in each output, while other cells remain unchanged. The destination color is associated with a prominent L-shaped connected component or analogous long bent line. Reported source→destination colors and changed-component areas: demo 1, 4→1 (15 cells); demo 2, 4→2 (4 cells); demo 3, 9→5 (11 cells); demo 4, 8→7 (6 cells); demo 5, 9→6 (8 cells); demo 6, 1→0 (7 cells); demo 7, 8→6 (3 cells); demo 8, 7→2 (11 cells). Area sometimes coincides with the key's area or an arm length, but not consistently; do not assume area matching is the selection rule. Infer the criterion from fresh examples and verify it against all available demonstrations before solving a recurrence.\n\nFailed test hypotheses to avoid repeating for the observed test: background 5; color-4 L component has 11 cells; color-3 components have sizes 3, 6, and 2; color-1 components have sizes 1, 2, and 1. Eight attempted transformations were all incorrect: recolor the color-4 L to 3; recolor all color-3 cells to 4; recolor the 6-cell color-3 component to 4; recolor the 3-cell color-3 component to 4; recolor the 2-cell color-3 component to 1; recolor the 1-cell color-1 domino to 4; again recolor the 2-cell color-3 component to 4; and recolor all color-1 cells to 4. These failures do not establish what the correct transformation is.","metadata":{"scope":"global","status":"unresolved","evidence":"eight demonstrations; one test instance with eight incorrect attempts"},"reason":"Correct the existing memory's unsupported solved-rule claim and retain the evidence and failure constraints for future recurrence.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_4d6ec835_recolor_designated_shape_match","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-4d6ec835: use the L key to recolor its designated shape match","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-4d6ec835. Identify the edge-touching L-shaped key component. Interpret the key's bounding-box pattern to find the reference component encoded by the non-key cells, then locate the separate designated component with exactly the same shape and recolor only that match to the key component's color. Preserve the key and all unrelated cells. Do not select incidental exact shape matches, such as dimers, without evidence that they are designated by the key pattern. Verified recurrence: the upper-right color-5 L enclosed a one-cell color-3 reference at row 0, column 19; the matching isolated color-3 cell at row 18, column 16 was recolored to 5. The accepted output changed only that target cell. Earlier guesses recoloring incidental dimers were incorrect.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"accepted test recurrence; earlier incidental-dimer guesses rejected"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:36:27.665Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:55:29.346Z","version":2},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_4d6ec835_recolor_designated_shape_match","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-4d6ec835: unresolved component recoloring associated with an L-shaped key","content":"Global task memory; rule unresolved. Across eight demonstrations, exactly one non-background connected component is recolored in each output, while other cells remain unchanged. The destination color is associated with a prominent L-shaped connected component or analogous long bent line. Reported source→destination colors and changed-component areas: demo 1, 4→1 (15 cells); demo 2, 4→2 (4 cells); demo 3, 9→5 (11 cells); demo 4, 8→7 (6 cells); demo 5, 9→6 (8 cells); demo 6, 1→0 (7 cells); demo 7, 8→6 (3 cells); demo 8, 7→2 (11 cells). Area sometimes coincides with the key's area or an arm length, but not consistently; do not assume area matching is the selection rule. Infer the criterion from fresh examples and verify it against all available demonstrations before solving a recurrence.\n\nFailed test hypotheses to avoid repeating for the observed test: background 5; color-4 L component has 11 cells; color-3 components have sizes 3, 6, and 2; color-1 components have sizes 1, 2, and 1. Eight attempted transformations were all incorrect: recolor the color-4 L to 3; recolor all color-3 cells to 4; recolor the 6-cell color-3 component to 4; recolor the 3-cell color-3 component to 4; recolor the 2-cell color-3 component to 1; recolor the 1-cell color-1 domino to 4; again recolor the 2-cell color-3 component to 4; and recolor all color-1 cells to 4. These failures do not establish what the correct transformation is.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","status":"unresolved","evidence":"eight demonstrations; one test instance with eight incorrect attempts"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:36:27.665Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:30:57.126Z","version":3},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/h