{"id":"refine_20260929143249063","summary":"Create a global memory for the verified frame-interior coloring rule in task-a923e602.","rationale":"Two demonstrations and an accepted test support filling closed frame interiors according to the parity of the frame dimensions; the test also showed that using color 2 for an odd-sized frame was incorrect.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, fill only the cells strictly inside each closed frame, choosing color 7 for odd-sized frames and color 2 for even-sized frames; preserve borders and unrelated cells, and validate dimensions and parity before submitting.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_a923e602_fill_frame_interiors_by_size_parity","title":"Continual-ARC task-a923e602: fill closed frame interiors by size parity","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-a923e602, supported by two demonstrations and a correctly solved test. Identify each closed hollow frame and its outer bounding-box dimensions. Fill only its enclosed interior cells, leaving the frame border and all other cells unchanged. Frames with odd side lengths (demonstrated 3×3, 5×5, and 7×7) receive color 7; frames with even side lengths (demonstrated 6×6) receive color 2. The border color is irrelevant. Preserve grid dimensions and background. In the test, color 2 in the odd 5×5 frame was incorrect; color 7 produced the accepted output. Check frame dimensions from the bounding box and change only cells strictly inside the border.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"This compact, verified task-specific rule should help solve future recurrences and records the failed odd-frame color choice to avoid repeating it.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_a923e602_fill_frame_interiors_by_size_parity","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-a923e602: fill closed frame interiors by size parity","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-a923e602, supported by two demonstrations and a correctly solved test. Identify each closed hollow frame and its outer bounding-box dimensions. Fill only its enclosed interior cells, leaving the frame border and all other cells unchanged. Frames with odd side lengths (demonstrated 3×3, 5×5, and 7×7) receive color 7; frames with even side lengths (demonstrated 6×6) receive color 2. The border color is irrelevant. Preserve grid dimensions and background. In the test, color 2 in the odd 5×5 frame was incorrect; color 7 produced the accepted output. Check frame dimensions from the bounding box and change only cells strictly inside the border.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:32:56.683Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:32:56.683Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929143413610","summary":"Update the existing task-451f745d memory with the verified 3×3 tile decoding rule, correcting its treatment of zero.","rationale":"The supplied demo and accepted test show that every aligned 3×3 tile reduces to its unique non-5 color; zero is a valid decoded output, not a value to ignore.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, produce one output cell per 3×3 tile in the same tile order, including zero-valued results, and verify each tile has exactly one non-5 color before submitting.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_451f745d_decode_3x3_blocks","title":"Continual-ARC task-451f745d: decode aligned 3×3 tiles by their unique non-5 color","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-451f745d, confirmed by a 15×15 demonstration and a correctly solved 27×27 test. Partition the input into aligned, non-overlapping 3×3 tiles. Each tile contains background color 5 and exactly one other color, or is uniformly that other color. Output a grid with one cell per tile, writing that tile’s unique non-5 color and preserving tile row and column order. Zero is a valid decoded color and must not be ignored. Before submitting, verify every tile has exactly one distinct color other than 5; if not, do not apply this rule without resolving the ambiguity from demonstrations.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The accepted test confirms the decoded output includes zero-valued tiles, superseding the prior instruction to ignore zero.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_451f745d_decode_3x3_blocks","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-451f745d: decode marker colors from 3×3 blocks","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-451f745d, confirmed by a demonstration and a correctly solved test. Partition the input into aligned, non-overlapping 3×3 blocks. Ignore values 0 and 5 as background/noise. For each block, output its unique remaining target color (observed colors include 2, 3, 4, 6, and 9), or 0 if none is present. Preserve block row/column order, producing dimensions one-third the input dimensions (for example, 24×24 becomes 8×8). Check that each block contains at most one distinct target color; treat conflicts as unresolved rather than guessing.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:16:56.230Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:02:06.996Z","version":3},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_451f745d_decode_3x3_blocks","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-451f745d: decode aligned 3×3 tiles by their unique non-5 color","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-451f745d, confirmed by a 15×15 demonstration and a correctly solved 27×27 test. Partition the input into aligned, non-overlapping 3×3 tiles. Each tile contains background color 5 and exactly one other color, or is uniformly that other color. Output a grid with one cell per tile, writing that tile’s unique non-5 color and preserving tile row and column order. Zero is a valid decoded color and must not be ignored. Before submitting, verify every tile has exactly one distinct color other than 5; if not, do not apply this rule without resolving the ambiguity from demonstrations.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:16:56.230Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:34:21.416Z","version":4},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929143653646","summary":"Updated the global task-4d6ec835 memory with the verified L-key template-matching rule.","rationale":"Two demonstrations and a correctly solved test establish that the L-shaped component encloses a smaller template whose exact shape and dimensions identify a separate object to recolor.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, identify the L-shaped key, confirm the template is inside its bounding rectangle, find the congruent external object regardless of its color, recolor only that object to the key color, and preserve all other cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_4d6ec835_recolor_designated_shape_match","title":"Continual-ARC task-4d6ec835: recolor the external object matching the L-key's enclosed template","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-4d6ec835, confirmed by two demonstrations and a correctly solved test. Find the prominent L-shaped component, formed by two perpendicular straight arms meeting at an endpoint. Inspect its bounding rectangle for a smaller object that serves as a shape template. Find a separate object elsewhere with exactly the same shape and dimensions, regardless of its color, and recolor only that external matching object to the L-shape's color. Preserve the L, the in-bounds template, and all other cells. Verify the template lies inside the L's bounding rectangle and distinguish it from the congruent external target. Evidence: a color-3 L enclosed a color-1 vertical four-cell template and the matching external color-8 object became 3; a color-1 L enclosed a color-6 vertical two-cell template and the matching external color-4 object became 1; a color-5 L enclosed a color-4 horizontal two-cell template and the matching external color-9 object became 5.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Replaces the previous unresolved guidance with the shape-selection rule supported by fresh demonstrations and a successful test.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_4d6ec835_recolor_designated_shape_match","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-4d6ec835: unresolved component recoloring associated with an L-shaped key","content":"Global task memory; rule unresolved. Across eight demonstrations, exactly one non-background connected component is recolored in each output, while other cells remain unchanged. The destination color is associated with a prominent L-shaped connected component or analogous long bent line. Reported source→destination colors and changed-component areas: demo 1, 4→1 (15 cells); demo 2, 4→2 (4 cells); demo 3, 9→5 (11 cells); demo 4, 8→7 (6 cells); demo 5, 9→6 (8 cells); demo 6, 1→0 (7 cells); demo 7, 8→6 (3 cells); demo 8, 7→2 (11 cells). Area sometimes coincides with the key's area or an arm length, but not consistently; do not assume area matching is the selection rule. Infer the criterion from fresh examples and verify it against all available demonstrations before solving a recurrence.\n\nFailed test hypotheses to avoid repeating for the observed test: background 5; color-4 L component has 11 cells; color-3 components have sizes 3, 6, and 2; color-1 components have sizes 1, 2, and 1. Eight attempted transformations were all incorrect: recolor the color-4 L to 3; recolor all color-3 cells to 4; recolor the 6-cell color-3 component to 4; recolor the 3-cell color-3 component to 4; recolor the 2-cell color-3 component to 1; recolor the 1-cell color-1 domino to 4; again recolor the 2-cell color-3 component to 4; and recolor all color-1 cells to 4. These failures do not establish what the correct transformation is.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","status":"unresolved","evidence":"eight demonstrations; one test instance with eight incorrect attempts"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:36:27.665Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:30:57.126Z","version":3},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_4d6ec835_recolor_designated_shape_match","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-4d6ec835: recolor the external object matching the L-key's enclosed template","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-4d6ec835, confirmed by two demonstrations and a correctly solved test. Find the prominent L-shaped component, formed by two perpendicular straight arms meeting at an endpoint. Inspect its bounding rectangle for a smaller object that serves as a shape template. Find a separate object elsewhere with exactly the same shape and dimensions, regardless of its color, and recolor only that external matching object to the L-shape's color. Preserve the L, the in-bounds template, and all other cells. Verify the template lies inside the L's bounding rectangle and distinguish it from the congruent external target. Evidence: a color-3 L enclosed a color-1 vertical four-cell template and the matching external color-8 object became 3; a color-1 L enclosed a color-6 vertical two-cell template and the matching external color-4 object became 1; a color-5 L enclosed a color-4 horizontal two-cell template and the matching external color-9 object became 5.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:36:27.665Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:36:58.984Z","version":4},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929144025605","summary":"Updated the global task-adc3b04d memory with the verified shared-color comparison rule and a coordinate-checking caution.","rationale":"The solved instance and three demonstrations confirm that aligned cells produce 3 only when both equal the panels’ shared color; every other pair produces that shared color. A one-cell transcription error caused the first submission to fail.","expectedOutcome":"On future recurrences, align the panels, infer their shared color, apply the rule cell by cell, and verify every output coordinate before submitting.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_adc3b04d_compare_panels_equal_cells","title":"Continual-ARC task-adc3b04d: compare aligned panel cells against the shared color","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-adc3b04d, confirmed by three demonstrations with horizontal and vertical separators and a correctly solved test. A solid line separates two equal-sized panels; omit the separator and align corresponding cells. Identify the color shared by the panels. Output 3 at a position only when both aligned input cells equal that shared color; otherwise output the shared color. Preserve panel dimensions and orientation. Carefully verify every coordinate: a manual one-cell transcription error caused an initial incorrect submission on the solved test.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Clarifies the demonstrated shared-color rule and preserves the evidenced lesson that coordinate-by-coordinate validation prevents transcription errors.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_adc3b04d_compare_panels_equal_cells","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-adc3b04d: mark equal aligned panel cells","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-adc3b04d, supported by eight demo pairs with horizontal and vertical dividers and a correctly solved test. Find the full single-color divider separating two equal-sized panels, remove it, and compare corresponding cells directly, without rotation or reflection. Write 3 where the aligned values are exactly equal; otherwise write the sole color shared by the two panels' palettes. Preserve the panel dimensions. Validation lesson: check every input row has its stated width and confirm the divider index and panel slices before comparing; a transcription omission can shift a panel and create false equality marks.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:18:05.143Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:18:05.143Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_adc3b04d_compare_panels_equal_cells","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-adc3b04d: compare aligned panel cells against the shared color","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-adc3b04d, confirmed by three demonstrations with horizontal and vertical separators and a correctly solved test. A solid line separates two equal-sized panels; omit the separator and align corresponding cells. Identify the color shared by the panels. Output 3 at a position only when both aligned input cells equal that shared color; otherwise output the shared color. Preserve panel dimensions and orientation. Carefully verify every coordinate: a manual one-cell transcription error caused an initial incorrect submission on the solved test.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:18:05.143Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:40:32.674Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
