rkers","content":"Global verified rule for Continual-ARC task-bc531327, supported by two demonstrations and a correctly solved test. Full straight divider lines partition the grid into a 3×3 array of equal-sized panels; panel dimensions can vary. Ignore the divider lines. Identify the uniform panel background and the distinct sparse marker color, then count markers separately in each panel. Output a 3×3 grid: use color 1 for panels containing exactly two markers, and use the original background color for every panel with any other count. Demonstrations confirmed the fallback depends on the background: with background 0, nonmatching panels output 0; with background 2, they output 2. In the solved test, the background was 7 and the marker was 0; only the center panel had exactly two markers, so only the center output cell was 1 and all others were 7. Do not substitute the marker color or always use zero for the fallback.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:48:02.907Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:48:02.907Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682293/attempts/52117ae0ff214dc5897fae72cc93757c/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
